# === Engine: MonoGame — undo the Unity block's project-file exclusions ===
# The "Engine: Unity" section above ignores *.csproj / *.sln. That is correct for Unity,
# which regenerates project files from its own asset database. It is WRONG for MonoGame:
# here the .csproj IS the project definition (target framework, NuGet refs, the pinned
# MonoGame 3.8.4.1 version, the MGCB content-pipeline hook). Without it, a fresh clone
# does not build at all. Re-include them.
!*.csproj
!*.sln
!*.slnx

# === Source directories the Unity build-output rules were eating ===
# `[Bb]uilds/` above (line ~53) is a Unity convention for compiled output. In THIS codebase
# `src/ResonanceHunter.Core/Builds/` is source — the character build system — and the rule
# swallowed it silently: the files sat on disk, the tests passed, `git status` said "clean",
# and a fresh clone would not have compiled. Same class of bug as the `*.csproj` rule above.
#
# Re-include source, and keep ignoring anything that is actually build output.
!src/**/Builds/
!tests/**/Builds/
